Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Name each model file explicitly, to mix precisions

`precision` picks one suffix for every model, so the int8 transformer
(flow_lm_main_int8.onnx, flow_lm_flow_int8.onnx) can't be combined with
the full-precision mimi_decoder.onnx. That combination is worth having:
the int8 transformer is ~4x smaller and faster, while decoder
quantization errors compound over a sentence (Kyutai keep the decoder
unquantized too), and in a listening test the full-precision decoder
sounded slightly better at little cost.

- Config gains text_conditioner_path, flow_lm_main_path,
  flow_lm_flow_path, mimi_decoder_path, mimi_encoder_path and bos_path.
  Empty (the default) keeps today's <models_dir>/<model>[_int8].onnx
  and the optional <models_dir>/bos_before_voice.npy; an explicit
  bos_path must be readable.
- C API ptt_create_from_files() takes each file's path. The encoder
  (only needed for WAV voices) and the BOS file may be NULL, and are
  then looked for next to flow_lm_main.
